Run.Description Aligned graphene on hBN, effective moire model: bands of one valley
Run.Prefix generate

# 55 x 55 graphene cells = one moire cell of aligned graphene on hBN (lattice mismatch -1/55)
Run.TypeOfSystem Graphene
Structure.CellSize 55
Structure.SuperCell 1
Moire.LatticePercent 0-0.018181818181818

# Effective moire model of Jung et al., Phys. Rev. B 89, 205414 (2014)
Moire.Potential .true.
Moire.Jeil .true.
Moire.H0AndHZ .true.
Moire.OffDiag .true.
Moire.OffDiagMidpoint .true.   # bond term at the bond midpoint: Hermitian Hamiltonian
Moire.PotC0   0-0.01013
Moire.PotCz   0-0.00901
Moire.PotCab  0.01134
Moire.PotPhi0  1.510233401750693
Moire.PotPhiz  0.147131255943122
Moire.PotPhiab 0.342084533390889

Kubo.Calc .false.
Diag.Calc .true.
Calculate.Bands .true.
MagField.Integer 0

# Plane-wave reduction: the Hamiltonian is projected on plane waves around one graphene valley
# (Diag.N_G = number of shells of moire reciprocal vectors; 8 shells = 55 vectors = 110 states)
TAPW.Use .true.
Diag.MoireAngle 0.0
Diag.N_G 8
Diag.UseKprimeValley .false.

Bands.NumPoints 40
&begin Bands.Path 4
0.0  0.0  0.0   # Gamma
1/3  2/3  0.0   # K: the corner of the moire zone where the Dirac point of this valley lies
1/2  1/2  0.0   # M
0.0  0.0  0.0   # Gamma
&end Bands.Path

Neigh.fastNNnotsquare .true.
Output.WriteDataFiles .false.
